{%- comment -%}
  XERO app — DELIBERATELY EMPTY. Do not restore until the app actually ships.

  This section rendered a simulated iPhone interface showing live telemetry: an
  estimated range, a battery state of health with a cycle count, brake pad wear, a
  "last check 4 min ago" timestamp and a torque figure that contradicted the rest of
  the site. None of it exists. It also carried a "Download for iPhone" call to action
  pointing at a placeholder link.

  The storefront states plainly that the companion app is in development and is not
  available at launch. A section asserting live vehicle telemetry directly contradicts
  that disclosure, and a download button for software that cannot be downloaded is a
  straightforward misrepresentation at the point of sale.

  The file stays because the Admin API cannot delete theme files - it can only
  overwrite them. The preset is gone, so it can no longer be added from the editor.

  If the app ships and this returns, every screen needs a visible caption reading
  "Simulated interface" unless it is a real screenshot, the figures must match the
  spec sheet, and the download link must point at a real App Store listing.
{%- endcomment -%}

